// An `is` test selects WHICH variant; the mutability comes from the SCRUTINEE,
// never from the type written in the test. Both variants here are read-only — the
// callback's type lends them so — and the narrowed `i32[]` is read-only too, so
// `push` is T3071 — reported on the push, at the right place, rather than swallowed
// by a T3040 "test can never match" on the test itself (which is what happened
// while the overlap check still compared mutability).
//
// The mirror case — a union of MUTABLE variants, where the same push is legal —
// is `tests/snippets/union_variant_narrow_mutation`.
module "snippet"

measure :: fn(f: fn(i32[] | string[]) -> void) -> void = f([1, 2])

main :: fn() -> i32 {
    measure((x: i32[] | string[]) -> {
        if x is i32[] {
            x.push(0)
        }
    })
    return 0
}
